# --- Browser stack (Phase 3): WPE WebKit + Cog, DRM/KMS at runtime ---
#
# BEST-EFFORT: these symbol names are not verified against an actual
# Buildroot 2026.05.1 checkout — there was no Linux host available to
# run menuconfig against this pinned version while writing this. If a
# name below is wrong, Buildroot silently drops it rather than erroring,
# so scripts/verify-browser-packages.sh checks the *resolved* .config
# for these exact symbols right after configuring and before the full
# build, so a bad name fails in seconds instead of after a multi-hour
# WPEWebKit build. Treat a first-run failure here as expected, not a
# regression; fix with `make O=$OUTPUT_DIR menuconfig` on Linux and
# `./scripts/save-defconfig.sh`.
#
# Iteration 1 (first real CI run) failed: BR2_PACKAGE_WPEWEBKIT/COG/
# COG_PLATFORM_DRM all failed to resolve, while the Mesa/DRM/EGL lines
# below resolved fine. Root cause per Buildroot's actual wpewebkit
# Config.in: WPEWebKit's own EGL implementation has a hard dependency
# on an EGL-capable Wayland backend (libwayland-egl), which we never
# enabled at all. This does NOT mean a Wayland compositor runs at
# runtime — Cog's DRM backend still owns the actual on-screen
# rendering via KMS, same as before. It's a build-time library
# dependency of WPEWebKit's EGL code, not a runtime architecture
# change; the "no X11/Wayland compositor" decision in
# docs/display-runtime-design.md still holds.
#
# Software rendering (Mesa llvmpipe via the swrast gallium driver) is
# the default because target hardware GPUs are unknown
# (docs/hardware-inventory.md is still all TBD) and there is no way to
# validate hardware-accelerated GL in the GitHub-hosted CI runners or
# the QEMU smoke test anyway. Once real target GPUs are known, revisit
# with a hardware driver (e.g. BR2_PACKAGE_MESA3D_GALLIUM_DRIVER_I915)
# as a per-device optimization, not a default.
BR2_PACKAGE_LIBDRM=y
BR2_PACKAGE_MESA3D=y
BR2_PACKAGE_MESA3D_OPENGL_EGL=y
BR2_PACKAGE_MESA3D_OPENGL_ES2=y
BR2_PACKAGE_MESA3D_GBM=y
BR2_PACKAGE_MESA3D_GALLIUM_DRIVER_SWRAST=y
BR2_PACKAGE_WAYLAND=y
BR2_PACKAGE_WAYLAND_PROTOCOLS=y
BR2_PACKAGE_WPEWEBKIT=y
BR2_PACKAGE_COG=y
BR2_PACKAGE_COG_PLATFORM_DRM=y
